# ============================================================================
# Line endings.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# core.autocrlf is true in this repository, so git converts text files to CRLF on
# checkout. That is fine for source, and it is what caused the encoding trouble in a
# different way, but it BREAKS SHELL SCRIPTS: sh cannot run a script whose lines end in
# CRLF, so the pre-commit hook would simply stop working after a fresh clone, silently.
#
# Only the shell scripts are pinned. Nothing else is declared, deliberately, so this file
# cannot cause a mass renormalisation of the whole repository.
# ============================================================================

# The git hooks run under sh, which requires LF.
scripts/githooks/* text eol=lf

# Any future shell script, wherever it lives.
*.sh text eol=lf
